WHO   — Turtles All The Way Down — Nested virtualization is real — VT-x can expose itself to a guest, so a VM can run a VM can run a VM. Embedding depth is unbounded in principle: a self-similar stack of machines, each believing it owns the hardware, each paying rent (performance) to the one below.
